WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.375
At the time the full extent
of his crimes became clear,

00:00:03.458 --> 00:00:05.750
in October 2012,

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:07.875
Jimmy Savile
was still revered

00:00:07.958 --> 00:00:09.333
as a British institution.

00:00:09.417 --> 00:00:10.792
His name was emblazoned

00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:13.167
throughout hospitals
across the UK.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.875
Streets were
named after him.

00:00:14.958 --> 00:00:16.917
But during the weeks
that followed,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.875
over a year
after his death in 2011,

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:21.417
Savile was revealed

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.833
as one of Britain's most
prolific sexual abusers.

00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:27.750
&lt;i&gt;That is a complete&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;flight of fantasy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:35.375
For those
that don't know him,

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:36.667
it's hard to articulate

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.125
exactly how famous
Savile was in the UK.

00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:41.667
His bleached hair,
gold jewellery,

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.083
and outlandish clothes
were cultivated

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.292
to make him stick
in the collective memory

00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:47.667
of the British people.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.792
When he rose to fame
in the 1980s,

00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:53.042
most UK presenters
spoke stiffly,

00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:54.250
in perfect English.

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:57.625
And as an unrefined miner
from a working-class area,

00:00:57.708 --> 00:01:00.208
Savile felt like a fresh,
genuine voice.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:02.042
Good morning, my sweetheart.

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:03.708
-How's things?
-Oh, alright.

00:01:03.792 --> 00:01:04.750
Give us a kiss, baby.

00:01:05.792 --> 00:01:07.167
He became as established

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.667
as the likes
of Oprah Winfrey

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:09.833
or David Letterman -

00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:11.292
the sort of household name

00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:13.417
whose fame
spanned generations.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.917
&lt;i&gt;A kind of private&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;pandemonium.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.500
Many parents grew up
listening to him on Radio 1,

00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:20.833
and their children watched
him on &lt;i&gt;Jim Will Fix It&lt;/i&gt;,

00:01:20.917 --> 00:01:25.500
a hugely popular show,
which ran from 1975 to 1994,

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:28.292
often receiving
20,000 letters a week

00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:30.417
from its enraptured
audience.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.625
Savile also presented
&lt;i&gt;Top of the Pops&lt;/i&gt;…

00:01:32.708 --> 00:01:33.875
Good evening,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:35.292
Welcome to &lt;i&gt;Top of the Pops&lt;/i&gt;.

00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:38.458
…a music show, which,
at its peak in the 70s,

00:01:38.542 --> 00:01:41.333
was watched
by 15 million people a week,

00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:42.625
around a quarter

00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:45.000
of the British population
at the time.

00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:47.625
But Savile's
novelty figure persona

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:49.458
hid horrific secrets.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.542
Over his 53-year career,

00:01:51.625 --> 00:01:54.083
Savile abused
countless victims,

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:56.333
aged five to 75.

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:57.458
After his death,

00:01:57.542 --> 00:02:00.792
over 450 people came forward
with allegations.

00:02:00.875 --> 00:02:02.708
Being able
to lock things away…

00:02:03.875 --> 00:02:05.000
was the way I coped.

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.417
His predatory behaviour
was allowed to flourish

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.917
for over five decades,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.167
and Savile's power
and calculating influence

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.625
meant that many accusations
about his behaviour

00:02:14.708 --> 00:02:16.833
were dismissed
as ridiculous.

00:02:16.917 --> 00:02:19.292
That sort of thing did
happen in the pop business.

00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:22.417
Savile was able to escape
justice for so long

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.333
because of his proximity
to influential people.

00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:28.542
It's difficult to reconcile
with his clownish persona,

00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:30.708
but he wielded
genuine power.

00:02:30.792 --> 00:02:31.875
He became synonymous

00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:34.375
with large demonstrative
charity projects,

00:02:34.458 --> 00:02:37.000
raising over
40 million pounds

00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:38.417
through events
that often gained

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.542
widespread media coverage.

00:02:40.625 --> 00:02:43.917
He was awarded
an OBE in 1972

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.958
and a knighthood in 1990,

00:02:46.042 --> 00:02:48.708
one of the highest honours
the Crown can bestow.

00:02:48.792 --> 00:02:49.917
No, it really is mine.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.458
-Are you sure?
-It's mine, I'm telling you.

00:02:51.542 --> 00:02:53.000
It's mine, yeah.
Tell him it's mine.

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:55.042
It is mine.
Thought I'd nicked it.

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:56.750
He was an unofficial adviser

00:02:56.833 --> 00:02:58.625
to members
of the royal family,

00:02:58.708 --> 00:02:59.917
the governor of Broadmoor,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.292
a high-security
psychiatric hospital,

00:03:02.375 --> 00:03:05.250
and an esteemed member
of the Catholic Church.

00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:07.542
He regularly dined
with Margaret Thatcher

00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:09.250
while she was
prime minister,

00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:12.417
and met the pope on his
visit to the United Kingdom.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.583
He was friends
with some of the most famous

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.375
musicians in the world.

00:03:16.458 --> 00:03:18.125
Governments, the monarchy,

00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:20.375
and established
British institutions,

00:03:20.458 --> 00:03:23.167
such as the BBC and NHS,

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.875
all trusted Savile.

00:03:24.958 --> 00:03:26.333
This place would
not be in existence

00:03:26.417 --> 00:03:28.542
without Jimmy Savile.

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:31.375
But his benevolent
persona was a lie,

00:03:31.458 --> 00:03:33.167
created to overshadow
the truth

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.750
about who and what he was.

00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:38.667
Some celebrities and
producers did raise concerns

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.458
about Savile's behaviour,

00:03:40.542 --> 00:03:41.750
but nothing ever came of it.

00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:43.625
And if they were ignored,

00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:46.167
there was even less chance
of hearing the voices

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.792
of the vulnerable,
disenfranchised people

00:03:48.875 --> 00:03:50.708
upon whom Savile prayed.

00:03:50.792 --> 00:03:52.250
The revelations about Savile

00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:54.792
led directly
to Operation Yewtree,

00:03:54.875 --> 00:03:58.250
a police investigation into
sexual abuse allegations,

00:03:58.333 --> 00:03:59.833
which led to the conviction

00:03:59.917 --> 00:04:01.583
of other British
celebrities,

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.042
such as Rolf Harris,
Gary Glitter,

00:04:04.125 --> 00:04:05.875
and Dave Lee Travis.

00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:08.042
You can watch the full story

00:04:08.125 --> 00:04:10.333
in &lt;i&gt;Jimmy Savile:&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;A British Horror Story&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:12.500
available on Netflix now.

00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:14.583
I am often tempted.

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.542
In fact, my case
comes up next Thursday.

